I've never tried it myself. I bet it hurts your leg.


> I like the idea of decorating corridors, it adds
> nicely to "dungeon dressing", but the other stuff
> you tossed in looks rejectable.

   I believe the point was that if you wallify corridors during dungeon
generation, the "tossed in" stuff comes free, and it would be a real
pain to specially remove it. That is, the code is /simpler/ and the
patch is smaller if you don't specially prohibit objects and traps in
open spaces that used to be unwallified corridors.

